Course name - Artificial intelligence and Data science

Programs
1.Basic Data Types
2.If-Else Statement
3.Loop and Array
4.Functions
5.Class and Object
6.Constructor and Destructor
7.Static Member
8.Inline and Friend Function

Brief Description
1.Basic Data Types – Demonstrates the use of int, char, and float data types in C++.
2.If-Else Statement – Demonstrates decision-making using an if-else statement to check whether a student has passed or failed.
3.Loop and Array – Demonstrates storing multiple values in an array and displaying them using a for loop.
4.Functions – Demonstrates creating and calling a function to perform addition of two numbers.
5.Class and Object – Demonstrates the basic concepts of classes and objects by storing and displaying student details.
6.Constructor and Destructor – Demonstrates the automatic execution of a constructor during object creation and a destructor during object destruction.
7.Static Member – Demonstrates the use of a static data member to count the number of objects created.
8.Inline and Friend Function – Demonstrates an inline function and a friend function for accessing and displaying private class data.
